B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=5{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-3{b}_{1}?$" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410059 1072 #uuid "1819c1f8-4cd2-5652-80f1-d185af0479c5" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410059 1074 "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={b}_{1}-5{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-5{b}_{2}+{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-(5{b}_{2})-(-{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-(5{b}_{2})-\\frac{1}{3}(-3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410060 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410053 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410060 1069 "q-112714" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410060 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410060 1071 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=\\frac{3}{4}{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=4{b}_{2}?$" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410060 1072 #uuid "be777f36-f8c5-5b1e-a52c-750939157337" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410060 1074 "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2}+3{b}_{3} \\\\  & =3{b}_{3}+2{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}(\\frac{3}{4}{b}_{3})-2\\cdot 3(-\\frac{1}{3}{b}_{1})-2(4{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-6{c}_{2}-2{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410061 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410051 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410061 1069 "q-35246" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410061 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410061 1071 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=-2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-3{b}_{1}?$" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410061 1072 #uuid "c92100bd-871b-5993-bed2-e255a4c7bcbb" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410061 1074 "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-2{b}_{2}+5{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-2{b}_{2}-\\frac{5}{3}(-3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}-\\frac{5}{3}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410062 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410055 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410062 1069 "q-81230" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410062 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410062 1071 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}?$" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410062 1072 #uuid "f46f0e34-3d5c-5e7a-9fb4-690993802dbe" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true] [17592186410062 1074 "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. By adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=2{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}={b}_{1}+(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =7{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\  & =7(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})+(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{7}{2}{c}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2} \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533588 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-003997e3-71e3-5fd0-8716-b578a050327a" 17592186410016 "answer-1787f492-78b1-512d-8267-7681cdc274c9" 17592186410017 "answer-1c013c9c-5216-521c-878e-e22df5716d0f" 17592186410018 "answer-20bb3464-f73d-5921-8cdf-f112ab14ead9" 17592186410019 "answer-252cd9d2-cd28-51d0-86dc-f100bfbf8425" 17592186410020 "answer-2ed8cf69-24dd-59de-9d4a-e94155db82e9" 17592186410021 "answer-36299c18-1f12-5691-a4cc-cf600875d435" 17592186410022 "answer-49d56a8d-fa50-583c-b245-a4a5b131b0c0" 17592186410023 "answer-4acab282-04ec-5eb0-ae3a-7ab839526ee4" 17592186410024 "answer-506dc288-02b9-55d3-a86e-0b1ffd046ff9" 17592186410025 "answer-54025de4-e25d-59ae-86a9-1ee27366fc6d" 17592186410026 "answer-5c547e71-e775-5595-94ae-8b1df8563107" 17592186410027 "answer-65ce31d1-a577-5b44-a7fa-3c3f399d7aa4" 17592186410028 "answer-75694ce1-5727-5971-a840-1a65ef92daf7" 17592186410029 "answer-7b46227a-c88c-5619-8cec-a1c99318b271" 17592186410030 "answer-7f7a28ee-dddd-5aff-9301-8500542e8d7c" 17592186410031 "answer-94609691-7cfa-58f9-b339-110e2b9cb3d1" 17592186410032 "answer-98bdd91b-9e6f-5202-91b7-08635ee7916f" 17592186410033 "answer-9e39fb95-43e2-541a-8451-cb5e1a8b5d30" 17592186410034 "answer-a0977355-df9c-5535-8046-cb1f92c60348" 17592186410035 "answer-a59b9759-c63d-5d7d-b9fb-807706aa26b0" 17592186410036 "answer-ad9fccc8-89c8-5084-95ed-898b492b9317" 17592186410037 "answer-af3b103c-e7ac-56f6-8025-6eee882f5637" 1759218641003